<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yolande, Duchess of Lorraine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1428–1483</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Yolande of Anjou</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yolande of Anjou was a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-of-anjou">René of Anjou</a> who inherited the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> in 1473. Her marriage to Ferry II of Vaudémont, son of René's old rival Antoine, reconciled the two branches of the house of Lorraine, and their son René II united Vaudémont with the duchy. She left the government of Lorraine to her son.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yolande-duchess-of-lorraine.jpg" alt="Yolande, Duchess of Lorraine" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis Boudan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dessin_du_vitrail_de_Yolande_d%27Anjou_aux_Cordeliers_d%27Angers_(d%C3%A9tail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
